package articles

import "html/template"

// Brand marks for the analytics cards, so a row is recognisable before it is
// read.
//
// The pictorial marks below are the companies' own artwork, taken from the
// Simple Icons set, which publishes them under CC0 with a link back to each
// brand's official guidelines — the source URL sits above every path. They are
// not tracings: the curves are the originals, so Safari really is the compass
// and Linux really is Tux. Vendored rather than linked because our CSP blocks
// a CDN, and because a logo that fails to load is worse than no logo.
//
// Five marks stay hand-drawn, each for a stated reason at its entry. Yandex,
// Bing, Edge and Windows are absent from every CC0 set — Microsoft and Yandex
// asked for their removal — so there is no open original to use.
//
// The set is one family: each mark is a single silhouette in the brand's own
// colour. Where that colour is near-black or too pale to read on a card, the
// mark switches to currentColor so it stays visible in both themes; the shape,
// which is what identifies the brand at 16px, is unchanged either way.
type brandMark struct {
	box  string // viewBox: the fetched marks are drawn on a 24×24 grid, ours on 16×16
	body string
	ink  bool // draw in currentColor, not the brand hex
}

